I built the Brief A phone agent and it passed all 10 practice customers in the final test run. That is one run, and a customer who passes once can fail the next time.

**Test runs** (one initial test, then the three fix rounds the skill allows):

| Run | Passed | Failed and why | What I changed |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 9/10 | PUB-10: the agent closed the call after the first failed `create_promise` instead of retrying. The error comes back in a form my result-handling code never sees. | Added a "retry once, without speaking" rule to the tool description and the prompt. |
| 2 | 8/10 | PUB-10: the judge counted the word "recorded" in the opening line. PUB-06: the agent offered the minimum payment twice and went back to the full amount after "too much". | Reworded the opening to "this call is kept on record". After "too much", every offer now uses the minimum amount. |
| 3 | 8/10 | PUB-04: the customer's sentence cut off at "the twenty" and the agent guessed the 20th. PUB-06: the minimum offer left out "the rest stays overdue". | The agent now asks again when a date is incomplete, and offers the deadline as an exact date. The minimum-payment offer is now a fixed sentence built in code. |
| 4 | **10/10** | none | |

**How it works:**
- **Code:** all date work is computed from `now`: business days, holidays, both deadlines, the "this/next weekday" table and the callback window. Each product's amounts, deadline and allowed persuasion attempts are also set in code.
- **Steps:** each step moves on only after a tool result, and every tool result tells the agent what to do next. The call ends in the end step right after `close_call`.
- **Prompt-only rules:** counting persuasion attempts and the retry of `create_promise` still depend on the prompt. These are the most likely to fail on a later run.

The workflow is generated by `out/build_brief_a.py`, which writes `out/brief-a.workflow.json`. Change the script and re-run it rather than editing the JSON by hand. Separately, the Google Drive connector needs to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings before it can be used.

